ood-prone locations is imminent or occurring. Rock falls are\noccuring in the steeper terrain.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 639 PM MDT, Doppler radar and automated rain gauges indicated\nheavy rain. Flooding is already occurring in the warned area.\nBetween 1 and 3.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 2 inches are possible in the\nwarned area.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nWolf Creek Pass and the creeks and streams flowing into the San\nJuan River.\n- Highway 160 over Wolf Creek Pass is closed due to flooding.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T03:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mineral, CO; Rio Grande, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5289a6353d07b40dfaad5f421c3d49793e9f3d0c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5289a6353d07b40dfaad5f421c3d49793e9f3d0c.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-23T05:28:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 230528 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1128 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flood Watch remains through the day Friday for the eastern San Juan mountains and the Upper Rio Grande Valley, with areal stream/river flooding and rock/mud slides possible. - Periods of moderate to heavy rain for the Continental Divide, tonight into early Friday","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&issuedby=PUB&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-10-22T06:48:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FLUS45 KPUB 220648 HWOPUB Hazardous Weather Outlook National Weather Service Pueblo CO 1248 AM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 COZ058>089-093>099-231300- Western Mosquito Range/East Lake County Above 11000 Feet- Leadville Vicinity/Lake County Below 11000 Feet- Eastern Sawatch Mountains Above 11000 Feet- Western Chaffee County Between 9000 and 11000 Feet- Central Chaffee County Below 9000 Feet- Western Mos","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=PUB&i